sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-goals-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In a 2D neural cellular automaton in which each cell only pursues metabolic (energy) homeostasis and is rewarded according to how well its stripe matches the pattern, evolution (ES-HyperNEAT) produced cell collectives with tissue-level setpoints that solve the French flag problem, i.e. organize a body-wide three-valued positional information axis.";
    dc:type "simulation-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evolution scales cell-level metabolic homeostasis into a tissue-level French flag axis";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Pio-Lopez L, Bischof J, LaPalme JV, Levin M, “The scaling of goals from cellular to anatomical homeostasis: an evolutionary simulation, experiment and analysis”, Interface focus (2023), doi:10.1098/rsfs.2022.0072; section “Abstract”. Scope: In silico 2D neural cellular automata with gap-junction signalling, evolved with ES-HyperNEAT"
}
